<!--
  The Android container's bridge (ADR-0006; android-runtime.md, sections 7.5
  and 10.2; the owner's decision of 15 November 2026). Fedora's Waydroid
  package puts waydroid0 in the "trusted" zone, which lets Android reach
  every service of the host. Binding the interface here first means that
  Waydroid's own "firewall-cmd -/-zone=trusted -/-add-interface" fails (the
  interface is already in a zone), and this zone applies instead.

  Towards the host, Android may only ask for an address (DHCP) and resolve
  names (DNS), both answered by Waydroid's dnsmasq on the bridge. Everything
  else addressed to the host is rejected: the zone's default target. Traffic
  to other networks is decided by the policy tur-android-out.
-->
<zone>
  <short>TUR Android</short>
  <description>The Android container: DHCP and DNS from the host, nothing else of the host.</description>
  <interface name="waydroid0"/>
  <service name="dhcp"/>
  <service name="dns"/>
</zone>
